From: lophophora <lsdphophora@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 19:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Always draw titlebar separator even in tools-area mode

Klassy suppresses the "Draw separator under titlebar" line whenever the
decoration is in tools-area mode, i.e. when the active colour scheme
defines a [Colors:Header] group (or "Match title bar color to
application color" is on). Most stock KDE colour schemes (BreezeLight
included) define Header colors, so the separator never shows on
normally-decorated windows like Dolphin, making the setting effectively
dead on such setups.

Drop the m_toolsAreaWillBeDrawn gate so the separator is drawn whenever
the option is enabled and the window is not shaded. The colour is still
only valid for active windows (titleBarSeparatorColor returns an invalid
colour otherwise), which matches the existing design.
---
 kdecoration/breezedecoration.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kdecoration/breezedecoration.cpp b/kdecoration/breezedecoration.cpp
index 2aabbf520..0e0af5020 100644
--- a/kdecoration/breezedecoration.cpp
+++ b/kdecoration/breezedecoration.cpp
@@ -2109,7 +2109,7 @@ qreal Decoration::titleBarSeparatorHeight(qreal scale) const
     // access client
     auto c = window();
 
-    if (m_internalSettings->drawTitleBarSeparator() && !c->isShaded() && !m_toolsAreaWillBeDrawn) {
+    if (m_internalSettings->drawTitleBarSeparator() && !c->isShaded()) {
         qreal height = 1;
         if (KWindowSystem::isPlatformX11())
             height *= m_systemScaleFactorX11;
